      "fallbackReason": null,
      "text": "How to Spot a Loser\n\n\nYou can always spot a Loser.\n\nYou see them binge eating cope after ordering from the menu of doubt.\n\nDoubt is cheap and tasty.\n\nAnd losers pick this every single time it’s on the menu.\n\nThe problem?\n\nIT IS ALWAYS ON THE MENU.\n\n\"Maybe it won’t work\"\n\n\"Maybe it’s too hard\"\n\n\"I doubt that works\"\n\nI’ll just have one of these please with some cope for dessert. \n\nThe only thing that makes them feel better after being too afraid to take monumental action is a nice large bowl of cope.\n\nThe \"average man\" is a gluttonous fat slob stuffing his face full of the stuff.\n\n\"Oh well I don’t wanna be rich anyway\"\n\n\"Money doesn’t buy happiness!\"\n\n\"It’s not my fault I failed, it was the economy\"\n\nYUMMMM.\n\nDelicious cope.\n\nWhen you ask why they order these things, they always have the same answer:\n\n\"Doubt and cope are cheap and they make me feel good\"\n\n\"Cope is super good, try some!\"\n\nBRUTAL MEDIOCRACY WITH A SUGAR COATING.\n\nThe cope makes you feel better but the world still thinks you’re a loser.\n\nThe world doesn’t care why you failed.\n\nThe world only cares that you DID FAIL.\n\nYOU DID NOT WIN.\n\nBECAUSE SOMEBODY ELSE DID.\n\nThere are luxury items on the menu of life. \n\nAnd luxury is often disguised in HARDSHIP.\n\nHard work, Pain and Suffering.\n\nIt will take some getting used to,\n\nHard work doesn’t always taste nice.\n\nPain, is bitter.\n\nSuffering has a horrible aftertaste.\n\nBut this clean diet of possibility is the menu of choice for every single champion.\n\nWhat COULD you be if you truly tried?\n\nHow hard would you try if you BELIEVED it could be done?\n\nHOW will the world respect you once you’ve MADE it?\n\nNo self-doubt.\n\nNo cope to feel better.\n\nJust bitter pain.\n\nHard work sets your throat on fire as you order more and more from the menu.\n\nAn all-you-can-eat buffet of capability that results in the highest echelon of excellence.\n\nThe building blocks to constructing a body and mind of fortitude and capability.\n\nYou are what you eat.\n\nMake the right choice.",
